# ─── AskLocker environment variables ──────────────────────────
# Copy to `.env` and fill in real values:  cp .env.example .env
# `.env` is gitignored and must never be committed.
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ─── Client (Expo) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Read by src/lib/supabase.ts. Anything prefixed EXPO_PUBLIC_ is
# INLINED INTO THE JS BUNDLE AT BUILD TIME and is publicly visible.
# Never put a secret behind this prefix — the anon key is safe here
# because Row-Level Security, not secrecy, is the access boundary.
# Get both from: Supabase dashboard > Project Settings > API
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-id.supabase.co
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key-here

# Optional — Google's own sign-in button on the web (src/lib/google-button.web.ts),
# so Google's screen names this app, not <project>.supabase.co. Public, like the
# anon key. Leave unset to keep the redirect sign-in everywhere.
# CLIENT_ID: the sign-in OAuth client (Google Cloud > APIs & Services >
#            Credentials) — the same one the Supabase Google provider uses.
# WEB_ORIGINS: the addresses listed in that client's Authorized JavaScript
#            origins, separated by commas, spaces or new lines (https:// may be
#            left out). Any other address (a preview) keeps the redirect
#            sign-in, because Google refuses an origin it was not told.
#            The login page says in the browser console which sign-in it uses.
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_WEB_ORIGINS=

# Optional — usage counts with PostHog (src/lib/analytics.ts): which screens
# and buttons are used, never a document, question, name or email.
# Production builds already send to AskLocker's own project (its key is in
# analytics.ts); every other build sends nothing. Set these only to send
# somewhere else, or to make a test build send.
# KEY: a PostHog project's API key ("phc_…", Project settings › General).
#      Public, like the anon key.
# HOST: where that project lives; EU Cloud unless set.
EXPO_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=
EXPO_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST=https://eu.i.posthog.com

# ─── Edge Function secrets (server-side only) ───────────────────
# NOT used by the app bundle and NOT read from this file. These live
# in Supabase and are set per project with:
#   supabase secrets set NAME=value --project-ref <ref>
# Listed here so the full set of required config is discoverable.
#
# SUPABASE_URL             - injected automatically by Supabase
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY - injected automatically by Supabase
#                             (full DB access; bypasses RLS)
# GROQ_API_KEY             - rag-search: Llama 3.3 70B answer generation
# HF_API_TOKEN             - ingest-document: all-MiniLM-L6-v2 embeddings
# OCR_SPACE_API_KEY        - ingest-document: server-side OCR fallback
# RAZORPAY_KEY_ID          - payments: Razorpay's API key id (rzp_test_… on DEV,
#                            rzp_live_… on PROD only). Unset: Plus is "coming soon"
# RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET      - payments: the key's secret; never leaves the server
# RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET  - razorpay-webhook: the secret typed into Razorpay's
#                            webhook settings
# RAZORPAY_CURRENCIES      - payments, optional: "INR" unless set; "INR,USD" once
#                            international payments are on in Razorpay

# ─── Local dev only ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# WEB_HOST - set automatically by Firebase Studio; read by app.config.ts
#            to allow the proxied preview origin through Expo's CORS
#            middleware. Leave unset everywhere else.
